{
  "id": "I-0074",
  "title": null,
  "body": "**FGA picSharp rewire LANDED (run 0008): route-(b) conventions + two standing caveats.**\n\nState after the rewire (`Picard/FGAPicRepresentability.lean`, **4 real `sorry`s**, all TRUE statements — Ground-verified run 0008 reconcile):\n\n- `picSharp C := PicSharp.relPresheaf C ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat` (`Type (u+1)`-valued, REAL). `Scheme.HasRationalPoint C` = Nonempty section subtype of `C.hom`; the ONE genuine FGA sorry is `instHasPicScheme [HasRationalPoint C]`. The other three are typed-sorry carriers: `PicSchemeLocallyOfFiniteType` (Kleiman §4 `th:main`(1), true under the rational point) and the pre-existing Quot-blocked `HasDivFunctor` / `HasAbelMap`.\n- `instPicSharpRepresentable` proved by `choose_spec`; `groupSchemeStructure : CommGrpObj (PicScheme C)` proved via `CommGrpObj.ofRepresentableBy` + a `Multiplicative.ofAdd` NatIso (`picSharpCommGrpForgetIso`, naturality is `rfl` — no defeq walls anywhere in this file).\n- Consumers: quantify over `[HasPicScheme C]` (synthesized from `[HasRationalPoint C]`) — `degree`/`kPoints_iff_kerDegree` in `IdentityComponent.lean` now carry it. `Pic0Scheme C := GroupScheme.IdentityComponent (PicScheme C)` is now a real def (axiom-clean), gated on `PicSchemeLocallyOfFiniteType`.\n\n**Caveat 1 — pointless curves:** `JacobianWitness` (`Jacobian.lean`) requires the abelian variety $J$ to exist UNconditionally, but route (b) only builds `PicScheme` for pointed $C$. For a genus-$\\ge 1$ curve without a rational point the eventual `picardJacobianWitness` proof needs Galois/étale descent from a finite extension where $C$ gains a point (or a pointed restatement of the north star). Not blocking anything now — record before anyone tries to close `picardJacobianWitness` directly.\n\n**Caveat 2 — `smoothProperQuotient` statement is WEAKER than Kleiman lm:qt and unprovable as stated:** Mathlib v4.31 has NO quasi-projectivity vocabulary, so hypothesis (2) of lm:qt is missing from the Lean statement; without it the statement is FALSE (Hironaka-type free ℤ/2 action on a smooth proper non-projective 3-fold: smooth proper equivalence relation, étale-quotient sheaf a non-scheme algebraic space). The former GLOBAL `instHasSmoothProperQuotient ⟨sorry⟩` (every presheaf representable!) was deleted this run (Ground-confirmed gone); the class is a use-site hypothesis only. Do NOT reintroduce a global instance, and do NOT try to prove the theorem as stated.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "author": "horizon",
      "body": "**Hygiene audit (janitor, 2026-07-25): the state snapshot in this memory is stale, but both caveats remain load-bearing — keeping open.**\n\nRe-checked `AJC/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/FGAPicRepresentability.lean` at HEAD:\n\n- The file now has **exactly one** code `sorry`: the conditional `instHasPicScheme` under `[HasRationalPoint C]` (the genuine FGA existence statement). The other three carriers listed above are gone — `instHasDivFunctor` is proved (witness `divFunctor C`), `instHasAbelMap` was repinned and closed, `instPicSchemeLocallyOfFiniteType` was absorbed. Read the \"4 real sorries\" paragraph as history.\n- **Caveat 1 (pointless curves) still applies:** `picardJacobianWitness` (`Jacobian.lean:185`) is unconditional while route (b) only builds `PicScheme` for pointed curves. No descent argument has landed.\n- **Caveat 2 still applies:** `HasSmoothProperQuotient` (`FGAPicRepresentability.lean:560`) is a use-site class with no global instance; the deleted `⟨sorry⟩` has not returned. Do not reintroduce it.",
      "created_at": null
    },
    {
      "author": "horizon",
      "body": "**Re-kinded `memory` → `protection` (janitor hygiene pass, run 0048). The body is unchanged.**\n\nRationale: the run-0008 state snapshot in the opening paragraphs is history (C-0001 already re-verified it at HEAD — `FGAPicRepresentability.lean` now carries exactly one `sorry`, the conditional `instHasPicScheme`). What is still load-bearing is *not* a durable fact but two standing constraints:\n\n1. **Do not close `picardJacobianWitness` directly** (`Jacobian.lean:185`): it is unconditional, while route (b) builds `PicScheme` only for a curve with a rational point. A genus-$\\ge 1$ curve without one needs Galois/étale descent from a finite extension where it acquires a point, or a pointed restatement of the north star.\n2. **Do not reintroduce a global `instHasSmoothProperQuotient`, and do not try to prove `smoothProperQuotient` as stated**: Mathlib v4.31 has no quasi-projectivity vocabulary, so hypothesis (2) of Kleiman lm:qt is missing and the statement is false as written (Hironaka-type free $\\mathbb{Z}/2$ action on a smooth proper non-projective threefold). The class is a use-site hypothesis only.\n\nBoth read as a soft freeze, so the item now renders in the Protected section — more visible to every run, and no longer competing for the ten-item memory budget with the live DD-R certificate memories. Revert with `inbox edit I-0074 --kind memory` if a human prefers it as memory.",
      "created_at": null
    },
    {
      "author": "human",
      "body": "PARTLY SUPERSEDED 2026-07-28 by the human etale-sheafify decision (protection I-0491) and its execution in run 0066 (task ajc-etale-pic, verified at HEAD).\n\nREAD THIS BEFORE ACTING ON THE BODY ABOVE. The body says the ONE genuine FGA sorry is instHasPicScheme [HasRationalPoint C]. That is no longer the state:\n * instHasPicScheme no longer exists AS AN INSTANCE. It survives as the sorry-free theorem picSchemeOfHasRationalPoint.\n * Scheme.HasRationalPoint still exists as a predicate, but the leaf hasRationalPoint_of_curve is DELETED — it was FALSE as stated, and nothing may consume or reprove it.\n * The representability obligation now lives on the ETALE-sheafified functor with NO rational-point binder: fgaPicardRepresentability in Picard/FGAPicRepresentability.lean, against Picard/PicEtSheaf.lean (262 lines, sorry-free, sheaf property proved).\n\nWHAT SURVIVES AND IS STILL BINDING: the route-(b) picSharp conventions, the Type (u+1)-valued relPresheaf shape, and the standing caveats about typed-sorry carriers (HasDivFunctor / HasAbelMap remain Quot-blocked). Those are unaffected by the decision.\n\nI am NOT editing this protection — an agent should not silently rewrite a standing constraint, and the conventions half is still live. Treat the state snapshot as HISTORY (it already carried one such correction from the run-0048 janitor pass) and the conventions as current. Authoritative present state: protection I-0491, roadmap AJC.picrep.rational-point, and run 0066s session report.",
      "created_at": null
    }
  ]
}

